9f76e0d-9ed5-55f1-b45e-726818fe959a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72527" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $y=-4x+1?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nThe line $y=-4x+1$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-4.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-6$ has a slope of $\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-6$ is perpendicular to the given line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72527/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29005c66-9f30-5862-926f-8a09320d404c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215890/selection/dc7ec60ff5b7a04a347aaf0aa27d9c463cb959555ca45dfa1b27ca6d79bd35b0" :answer/id #uuid "336c559d-12e9-5d41-a518-3be48a3474b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215890/selection/f7729a84b57ba7dcc71127e7ae01453471dd30e4d18e34e798e450f6edaf268e" :answer/id #uuid "542fe3ee-11c7-52fc-9bc9-64df371b415e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215890/selection/76ab007d3a08a842d5701fcb3c77f582058ebb778aebfc66175c041330c90208" :answer/id #uuid "f7688e72-d922-592b-91bf-8da17faaf359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215890/selection/e0e2e006118b554e24734e2727ff3108130d0b6afc6cdcbcd92544f235351c71" :answer/id #uuid "7fda33cf-703e-5154-a538-ec45393954ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215890/selection/f2828f07b83d9a718355f6f154ad27c8f354f4ed674a9ad6fa4431e4c5f838fd" :answer/id #uuid "aaaa58