lar to $y=-5x-2?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nThe line $y=-5x-2$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-5.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=\\frac{1}{5}x-8$ has a slope of $\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=\\frac{1}{5}x-8$ is perpendicular to the given line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72528/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29005c66-9f30-5862-926f-8a09320d404c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72524/selection/100b0c61d8a1ebeec3152082d7c36c28ccbef8ca9163774c062610608872d154" :answer/id #uuid "ef2b93d7-0036-5099-853f-a69da6437feb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72524/selection/9e41e6bdca33da5366da16e5cbcff188b6888c2989890f800a7cce5c7a294588" :answer/id #uuid "edd37f4f-34cf-522a-ad44-6ac435d82980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{x}{2}x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72524/selection/7f582cbc39cf0522fa365f2e3c701a68d9908c6d395652c8001c8cdfb4121fcd" :answer/id #uuid "8a2e581c-4b90-5956-915f-73b3665fd911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{x}{2}x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72524/selection/a20e462a24b2d65cab7429839bc46b524d25f7f1678fb82590234c6d14c4d796" :answer/id #uuid "05c1c39f-dcf4-5a73-812f-6620edf83def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72524/selection/dcbc5f145587d239688f32f8aef4253c067b02124bcbe0d181862500d27c95c0" :answer/id #uuid "157724cd-8632-5718-9979-7dd1e56872b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72524/selection" :answer-f