in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-1.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=x+3$ has a slope of $1.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot 1=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=x+3$ is perpendicular to the given line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215888/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29005c66-9f30-5862-926f-8a09320d404c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763/selection/ce8527206d007839d442d2c67ea9ed494d31fcecbd03a6266fc6ece56b6cbde8" :answer/id #uuid "0704705c-f701-5e9e-848d-012eeb8fa1b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763/selection/76ab007d3a08a842d5701fcb3c77f582058ebb778aebfc66175c041330c90208" :answer/id #uuid "7f4a9087-5733-5704-931e-6c8283f22530" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763/selection/861981e024e897416682817ca9e79c6d1e8ed9b541c7efe134d14879c4bffd37" :answer/id #uuid "bc77c2f3-14a8-58d8-97f8-c8ec1c068095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763/selection/e0b9935198f3feca3a4ac4537deff114f72a5eb396c605dec273a5f677d2a096" :answer/id #uuid "57940993-3ab1-59d3-af05-10f54fa0fb1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763/selection/0db32750223419c0445a3c8e2f10be0ab1fbdae0b1da1e58b3d34a193fa0c9f3" :answer/id #uuid "c8056b55-bf4f-56b1-8714-902c3a23a9a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6bd3f21-fdc6-5b29-8b89-b8bbabc51ff7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-59763/selection/e0b9935198f3feca3a4ac4537deff114f72a5eb396c605dec273a5f677d2a096" :answer-field/choices ["q-59763/selection/ce8527206d007839d442d2c67ea9ed494d31fcecbd03a6266fc6ece56b6cbde8" "q-59763/selection/76ab007d3a08a842d5701fcb3c77f582058ebb778aebfc66175c041330c90208" "q-59763/selection/861981e024e897416682817ca9e79c6d1e8ed9b541c7efe134d14879c4bffd37" "q-59763/selection/e0b9935198f3feca3a4ac4537deff114f72a5eb396c605dec273a5f677d2a096" "q-59763/selection/0db32750223419c0445a3c8e2f10be0ab1fbdae0b1da1e58b3d34a193fa0c9f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-59763" :question/id #uuid "7df21e4b-12cf-5842-bae2-b10ce1dbd5d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-59763" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $4x+2y=8?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $4x+2y=8,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2y & =8 \\\\ 2y & =-4x+8 \\\\ y & =-2x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $-2.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+5$ has a slope of $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+5$ is perpendicular to the given line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-59763/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e732f270-1d6f-5ff8-8792-d9b329ea858d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-59763"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-44404"] :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $x+5y=10,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =10 \\\\ 5y & =-x+10 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{5}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $-\\frac{1}{5}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=5x-4$ has a slope of $5.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot 5=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=5x-4$ is perpendicular to the given line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-23618/selection/a593ce81680e4a015bacc42119f2d1f6f2b564df9824260f991bffc91603cba1" :answer/id #uuid "c739c91d-86c2-56ab-b6ef-3e5c5142165c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-8x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23618/selection/f538d7c2bd89d8206ab512906706b2d5d9f6316273047c64ecfeec0c2fcff4b9" :answer/id #uuid "e1007cc1-c24f-575a-86ee-486678a222c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{8}x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23618/selection/bf4174198f5b686fea6f864facfb1133228aa751c5ea65b5d39d7b2e4b15d407" :answer/id #uuid "1f13ede2-082f-5b19-8ecb-fbfe40e026d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{8}x+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23618/selection/6d8621f915b83621df1df6b087c63560b12ee9c78b1a41c642fcb26a50b2812d" :answer/id #uuid "0ccb436d-05f7-54c7-baf2-c8248f5fbefe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23618/selection/435f111f1b7742befe592d4572ba318df03f77a5578d08c3a4542d08577ef290" :answer/id #uuid "6c1bc78d-e1cd-5c68-9cad-4cef1425025c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23618/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a1c68d-8f5e-5fb7-866a-059b815ef7b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-23618/selection/bf4174198f5b686fea6f864facfb1133228aa751c5ea65b5d39d7b2e4b15d407" :answer-field/choices ["q-23618/selecti