aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of $4y+3px=0,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y+3px & =0 \\\\ 4y & =-3px \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3p}{4}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- The slope of the line $15x+5y=9$ is $-3.$\n\n- The slope of the line $4y+3px=0$ is $-\\frac{3p}{4}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-3)\\cdot -\\frac{3p}{4}=-1\\,⟹\\,p=-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-44515/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f3d7d62-686b-59c4-9ea1-695c6be3180b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-44515"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "563ac7fd-1f06-5355-b267-40dadd1c8538" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "98db34bb-d034-58bc-8046-fd201e22300d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "0e929f4a-f1bb-5ab4-83e5-d24448ccd926" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "0774c27a-c36e-53ec-bd96-d01ba66699e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "12dc05e7-1780-5094-b59e-0f2063438ecd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86ed7e8c-a30e-5b3f-9e79-44d994e1a548" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-44407/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-44407/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-44407/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-44407/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-44407/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-44407/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-44407" :question/id #uuid "b7b2fbae-964a-51a8-a3e9-de9e38e6e854" :question/math-academy-id "q-44407" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The lines $4x-8y=7$ and $3y-px=9$ are perpendicular. The value of $p=$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of $4x-8y=7,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y & =7 \\\\ -8y & =-4x+7 \\\\ 8y & =4x-7 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of $3y-px=9,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y-px & =9 \\\\ 3y & =px+9 \\\\ y & =\\frac{p}{3}x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- The slope of the line $4x-8y=7$ is $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The slope of the line $3y-px=9$ is $\\frac{p}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{p}{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,p=-6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-44407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f3d7d62-686b-59c4-9ea1-695c6be3180b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-44407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215941/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "4bdb4b9f-e6e9-50b7-96d7-b2f9da7cadb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215941/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2feff926-444f-55b2-8a81-15eea93cb07d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215941/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-215941/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215941" :question/id #uuid "dedc61d6-f231-5dad-bf68-62d6505aac80" :question/math-academy-id "q-215941" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The lines $y=-5x+3$ and $3kx-5y=9$ are perpendicular. What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\n- The first line is in slope-intercept form, and the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So the slope of the line $y=-5x+3$ is $-5.$\n\n- To find the slope of $3kx-5y=9,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3kx-5y & =9 \\\\ 5y & =3kx-9 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3k}{5}x-\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line $3kx-5y=9$ is $\\frac{3k}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-5)\\cdot (\\frac{3k}{5})=-1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-215941/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f3d7d62-686b-59c4-9ea1-695c6be3180b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215941"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-28328/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "88f59d34-c649-5a28-9146-a9ae12057a18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28328/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "0d7e130e-0517-5fbf-a835-96bee6ce4183" :answer/typ